  "selected": "row-reuse",
  "reason": "Reuse ordinary eight-bit filtered buffers for native samples and cap on-demand inflation growth requests at the output limit. Repeated photo decode +5.28% relative to Rust png (unchanged reader +1.86%); format decode +10.28% (reader +0.26%) and raw inflate +18.36% relative to flate2 (unchanged streaming +2.78%). Photo raw inflation is inconclusive. Exact native bytes agree on 84 inputs; cohort capacities show lower inflation storage and removal of the second full byte-sample buffer. Shared-host measurements do not prove broad parity. Longer checks clear the original PNG regressions, but stored-only gray8 Adam7 raw inflation remains 9.02 to 11.02 microseconds, -28.49% relative to flate2 and -12.03% relative to unchanged streaming inflation. Retain this explicit allocation/throughput tradeoff; no uniform raw-inflate speedup is claimed.",
  "production_sources_changed": [
    "src/apng.rs",
    "src/codec.rs",
    "src/scanline.rs",
    "src/zlib.rs"
  ],
